%% Theory-session flow with durable asynchronous answer evaluation.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Candidate as User
    participant API as NestJS Theory API
    participant Clerk as Clerk token verification
    participant Redis as Redis quota counter
    participant Mongo as MongoDB question bank
    participant PG as PostgreSQL sessions and answers
    participant Queue as BullMQ theory-eval queue
    participant Worker as Theory evaluation worker
    participant Mastra as Theory evaluator agent
    participant Router as NVIDIA primary / Groq fallback

    Candidate->>API: POST /api/v1/theory/session/start
    API->>Clerk: Verify Bearer token
    Clerk-->>API: Clerk user ID
    API->>Redis: Atomically reserve daily session quota
    alt Quota reached
        Redis-->>API: Rejected
        API-->>Candidate: HTTP 403 quota limit
    else Quota available
        Redis-->>API: Reservation granted
        API->>PG: Create session
        PG-->>API: Session
        API-->>Candidate: Session created
    end

    Candidate->>API: POST /api/v1/theory/session/:id/answer
    API->>PG: Verify session ownership
    API->>PG: Transactionally reserve slot and persist queued answer
    alt Session full or no longer active
        PG-->>API: Reservation rejected
        API-->>Candidate: HTTP 409 session cannot accept answer
    else Slot reserved
        PG-->>API: Queued answer ID
        API->>Queue: Enqueue deterministic evaluation job
        API-->>Candidate: HTTP 202 queued answer and ID
        Worker->>PG: Mark answer running and load answer data
        Worker->>Mastra: Generate structured score and feedback
        Mastra->>Router: Evaluate answer
        alt NVIDIA fails and Groq is configured
            Router->>Router: Retry with Groq
        end
        Router-->>Mastra: Structured score and feedback
        Mastra-->>Worker: Evaluation result
        Worker->>PG: Persist score, feedback, provider, model and prompt version
        Candidate->>API: GET session/:id/answers/:answerId
        API->>PG: Verify owner and read persisted answer state
        PG-->>API: queued/running/completed/failed result
        API-->>Candidate: HTTP 200 evaluation status
    end
